WEBVTT

00:00:00.411 --> 00:00:02.771
Oxford Bookworm's Library.

00:00:02.832 --> 00:00:04.512
Starter.

00:00:04.572 --> 00:00:07.723
The Girl with Green Eyes.

00:00:07.783 --> 00:00:10.143
By John Escott.

00:00:10.203 --> 00:00:13.564
Read by Christopher Ragland.

00:00:13.624 --> 00:00:26.206
Published and copyright, Oxford University Press 2012.

00:00:26.266 --> 00:00:37.689
the girl with green eyes.

00:00:37.749 --> 00:00:44.834
Greg is a porter at the Shepton Hotel in New York.

00:00:44.894 --> 00:00:52.290
After work, he always goes for a coffee across the street.

00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:58.674
A girl is sitting in the coffee shop near the window.

00:00:58.734 --> 00:01:03.588
It's her again, thanks Greg.

00:01:03.648 --> 00:01:07.720
She's here every afternoon.

00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:11.762
I'm going to say hello.

00:01:11.822 --> 00:01:18.646
Greg goes into the coffee shop and gets a coffee.

00:01:18.706 --> 00:01:24.240
Then he goes across to the girl's table.

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:27.823
Hi, he says.

00:01:27.883 --> 00:01:30.074
I'm Greg.

00:01:30.134 --> 00:01:33.182
Can I sit with you?

00:01:33.242 --> 00:01:40.172
Okay, she says, I'm Cassie.

00:01:40.232 --> 00:01:47.746
I come here for a coffee every day after work, says Greg.

00:01:47.806 --> 00:01:52.370
I'm a porter at the Shepton Hotel.

00:01:52.430 --> 00:01:54.810
He smiles.

00:01:54.870 --> 00:01:59.553
You have beautiful green eyes.

00:01:59.613 --> 00:02:01.654
Have I?

00:02:01.714 --> 00:02:03.738
She says.

00:02:03.798 --> 00:02:07.394
She doesn't smile.

00:02:07.454 --> 00:02:11.056
Is something wrong, Cassie?

00:02:11.116 --> 00:02:13.097
He asks.

00:02:13.156 --> 00:02:17.090
You don't look very happy.

00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:23.642
It, it's nothing, she says.

00:02:23.702 --> 00:02:31.058
Tell me, says Greg, maybe I can help.

00:02:31.118 --> 00:02:35.274
Well, She begins.

00:02:35.334 --> 00:02:39.376
Go on, says Greg.

00:02:39.436 --> 00:02:47.062
My stepfather is staying at the Shepton Hotel, she says.

00:02:47.122 --> 00:02:50.534
He has my sketchbooks.

00:02:50.594 --> 00:02:53.606
I'm an artist.

00:02:53.666 --> 00:02:59.718
When I ask him to give them to me, he says, no.

00:02:59.778 --> 00:03:05.098
I want you to come back home to Boston.

00:03:05.158 --> 00:03:09.981
But I don't want to go back to Boston.

00:03:10.041 --> 00:03:13.133
He's not nice.

00:03:13.193 --> 00:03:18.226
How long is he going to be at the hotel?

00:03:18.286 --> 00:03:20.418
asked Greg.

00:03:20.478 --> 00:03:25.320
Two more days, says Cassie.

00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:29.300
He's in room 724.

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:36.752
Maybe I can get the sketchbooks for you, says Greg.

00:03:36.812 --> 00:03:41.256
Maybe I can get into his room.

00:03:41.316 --> 00:03:43.437
Can you?

00:03:43.497 --> 00:03:45.568
She says.

00:03:45.628 --> 00:03:53.484
Meet me here tomorrow afternoon at 4.30, says Greg.

00:03:53.544 --> 00:03:55.384
Okay.

00:03:55.444 --> 00:03:59.344
Thank you, says Cassie.

00:03:59.403 --> 00:04:02.892
Thank you very much.

00:04:02.952 --> 00:04:06.014
She looks at her watch.

00:04:06.074 --> 00:04:08.946
I've got to go now.

00:04:09.005 --> 00:04:12.448
See you tomorrow.

00:04:12.508 --> 00:04:21.473
When Cassie gets back to her hotel room, she makes a telephone call.

00:04:21.532 --> 00:04:23.514
Hello?

00:04:23.574 --> 00:04:25.416
She says.

00:04:25.476 --> 00:04:27.494
It's me.

00:04:27.554 --> 00:04:29.784
It's okay.

00:04:29.844 --> 00:04:32.966
The boy's going to do it.

00:04:33.025 --> 00:04:34.868
Yes.

00:04:34.928 --> 00:04:40.442
I'm going to get them from him tomorrow afternoon.

00:04:40.502 --> 00:04:42.434
Okay.

00:04:42.494 --> 00:04:48.308
I can meet you there the morning after at 10 a.m.

00:04:48.367 --> 00:04:51.480
Don't forget to bring the money.

00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:55.329
$2,000.

00:04:55.389 --> 00:05:02.850
Next morning, Greg arrives at work early.

00:05:02.910 --> 00:05:08.554
He goes to find room 724.

00:05:08.614 --> 00:05:18.149
I have to wait for Cassie's stepfather to go out, he thinks.

00:05:18.169 --> 00:05:24.084
I don't know his name, but it doesn't matter.

00:05:24.143 --> 00:05:30.939
Greg watches the door of room 724.

00:05:30.998 --> 00:05:37.742
He sees the girl come to clean the rooms.

00:05:37.802 --> 00:05:47.568
Some minutes later, a man comes out of room 724.

00:05:47.628 --> 00:05:54.653
That must be Cassie's stepfather, thinks Greg.

00:05:54.713 --> 00:06:06.540
He waits for the man to leave, and for the cleaning girl to go into room 724.

00:06:06.600 --> 00:06:12.584
I need to look in the room, he thinks.

00:06:12.644 --> 00:06:18.268
Greg waits for the girl to leave the bedroom.

00:06:18.328 --> 00:06:26.560
Then He goes into the room and begins to look for the sketchbooks.

00:06:26.620 --> 00:06:31.152
I must be quick, he thinks.

00:06:31.212 --> 00:06:34.242
Where are they?

00:06:34.302 --> 00:06:41.556
Suddenly Greg sees the sketchbooks by the bed.

00:06:41.616 --> 00:06:45.598
Got them, he thinks.

00:06:45.658 --> 00:06:50.189
He begins to look at the pictures.

00:06:50.249 --> 00:06:52.378
Wow!

00:06:52.438 --> 00:06:56.400
Cassie is a great artist!

00:06:56.460 --> 00:06:59.862
These are good!

00:06:59.922 --> 00:07:08.576
Greg is leaving the room when he hears the cleaning girl call out to him.

00:07:08.636 --> 00:07:10.546
Hey!

00:07:10.606 --> 00:07:12.368
She says.

00:07:12.427 --> 00:07:15.068
What are you doing?

00:07:15.128 --> 00:07:17.530
Come back!

00:07:17.590 --> 00:07:22.132
Greg does not stop.

00:07:22.191 --> 00:07:32.604
Greg finishes work that afternoon and leaves the hotel through a door in the next street.

00:07:32.664 --> 00:07:43.326
When he gets near the front of the hotel, he sees the man from room 724.

00:07:43.386 --> 00:07:48.206
That's him again, thinks Greg.

00:07:48.266 --> 00:07:52.130
That's Cassie's stepfather.

00:07:52.190 --> 00:07:57.727
Greg waits for the man to go into the hotel.

00:07:57.786 --> 00:08:02.820
Then he goes to the coffee shop.

00:08:02.880 --> 00:08:09.736
Cassie is at the same table in the coffee shop.

00:08:09.796 --> 00:08:16.070
Greg gets a coffee and goes to sit with her.

00:08:16.130 --> 00:08:19.894
I have them, he says.

00:08:19.954 --> 00:08:24.508
and he puts the sketchbooks on the table.

00:08:24.568 --> 00:08:29.451
That's great, says Cassie.

00:08:29.510 --> 00:08:33.243
How can I thank you, Greg?

00:08:33.303 --> 00:08:44.810
You can meet me later, he says, after I go home and change out of my porter's uniform.

00:08:44.870 --> 00:08:50.146
I'm sorry, Greg, says Cassie.

00:08:50.206 --> 00:08:52.839
I can't tonight.

00:08:52.898 --> 00:08:56.319
Maybe tomorrow night.

00:08:56.379 --> 00:08:59.940
Okay, says Greg.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:02.090
Tomorrow night.

00:09:02.150 --> 00:09:06.201
We can get something to eat first.

00:09:06.261 --> 00:09:11.002
Yes, okay, says Cassie.

00:09:11.062 --> 00:09:19.296
I have to go now, but meet me here tomorrow evening at six o'clock.

00:09:19.356 --> 00:09:24.000
Cassie gets up, ready to leave.

00:09:24.060 --> 00:09:29.004
Don't forget your key, says Greg.

00:09:29.064 --> 00:09:35.298
Oh, thanks, says Cassie.

00:09:35.358 --> 00:09:38.550
She takes it from him quickly.

00:09:38.610 --> 00:09:41.663
See you tomorrow.

00:09:41.723 --> 00:09:49.726
Greg is finishing his coffee when he sees his friend, Mike.

00:09:49.786 --> 00:09:54.896
You're in trouble, Greg," says Mike.

00:09:54.956 --> 00:10:00.317
Jake Russo's sketchbooks are not in his room.

00:10:00.377 --> 00:10:04.118
Room 724.

00:10:04.178 --> 00:10:12.810
And there are CCTV pictures of you coming from that room.

00:10:12.870 --> 00:10:17.231
Who is Jake Russo?

00:10:17.291 --> 00:10:19.328
asks Greg.

00:10:19.388 --> 00:10:24.300
Suddenly, he's not feeling very well.

00:10:24.360 --> 00:10:28.815
An artist, says Mike.

00:10:28.875 --> 00:10:38.640
His pictures sell for thousands of dollars, and his sketchbooks sell for thousands too.

00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:41.716
Do you have them?"

00:10:41.776 --> 00:10:44.777
asks Mike.

00:10:44.797 --> 00:10:45.358
No.

00:10:45.418 --> 00:10:50.699
A girl has them, says Greg.

00:10:50.759 --> 00:10:52.930
What girl?

00:10:52.990 --> 00:10:55.080
asks Mike.

00:10:55.140 --> 00:11:00.332
A girl with green eyes, says Greg.

00:11:00.392 --> 00:11:05.962
And he tells Mike about Cassie and her stepfather.

00:11:06.022 --> 00:11:13.926
But it's not true," says Mike, when Greg finishes speaking.

00:11:13.986 --> 00:11:20.382
Jake Russo doesn't have a wife or a stepdaughter.

00:11:20.442 --> 00:11:26.628
You have to find that girl and get the sketchbooks, Greg.

00:11:26.688 --> 00:11:32.566
And you have to do it before the police find you.

00:11:32.626 --> 00:11:38.842
Greg walks home to his one room apartment.

00:11:38.902 --> 00:11:42.866
How am I going to find her?

00:11:42.926 --> 00:11:44.916
He thinks.

00:11:44.976 --> 00:11:54.703
She has Jake Russo's sketchbooks now, so she's not going to meet me again.

00:11:54.763 --> 00:12:00.555
Is she going to sell them for a lot of money?

00:12:00.616 --> 00:12:09.020
There is a police car in the street next to Greg's apartment.

00:12:09.080 --> 00:12:14.133
Oh no, he thinks.

00:12:14.193 --> 00:12:17.356
They're waiting for me.

00:12:17.416 --> 00:12:22.719
I can't get into my apartment now.

00:12:22.779 --> 00:12:30.260
That night, Greg sleeps on a train in the subway.

00:12:30.320 --> 00:12:33.968
But early the next morning...

00:12:34.028 --> 00:12:36.248
Hey you!

00:12:36.308 --> 00:12:38.499
Says a man.

00:12:38.559 --> 00:12:41.840
He's the subway cleaner.

00:12:41.900 --> 00:12:43.891
Get up!

00:12:43.951 --> 00:12:48.432
You can't sleep here all day!

00:12:48.492 --> 00:12:53.204
Sorry, says Greg.

00:12:53.264 --> 00:12:59.393
People are arriving to get their trains now.

00:12:59.453 --> 00:13:10.814
One of them stops and looks at a photograph in his newspaper and then at Greg.

00:13:10.874 --> 00:13:15.625
It's him, thinks the man.

00:13:15.685 --> 00:13:21.627
It's the young man in the newspaper photograph.

00:13:21.687 --> 00:13:26.869
The police are looking for him.

00:13:26.929 --> 00:13:33.901
Suddenly, Greg sees the man looking at him.

00:13:33.961 --> 00:13:41.242
And he sees his picture on the front of the man's newspaper.

00:13:41.302 --> 00:13:47.874
I have to get out of here quickly, he thinks.

00:13:47.934 --> 00:13:54.454
The man with the newspaper finds a policeman.

00:13:54.514 --> 00:13:56.785
It's him.

00:13:56.845 --> 00:14:00.186
He tells the policeman.

00:14:00.246 --> 00:14:04.126
The hotel porter.

00:14:04.186 --> 00:14:07.298
Hey, you!

00:14:07.358 --> 00:14:11.308
The policeman calls to Greg.

00:14:11.368 --> 00:14:14.900
Greg runs.

00:14:14.960 --> 00:14:17.350
Stop!

00:14:17.410 --> 00:14:20.401
Calls the policeman.

00:14:20.461 --> 00:14:24.566
Greg doesn't stop.

00:14:24.626 --> 00:14:29.302
I have to get out of this uniform.

00:14:29.362 --> 00:14:31.614
Thanks, Greg.

00:14:31.674 --> 00:14:35.858
People know I'm the porter.

00:14:35.918 --> 00:14:42.402
Maybe Mike can give me something different to wear.

00:14:42.462 --> 00:14:49.717
When he gets to Mike's apartment, Mike opens the door.

00:14:49.777 --> 00:14:53.630
I need something to wear.

00:14:53.690 --> 00:14:56.141
Greg tells him.

00:14:56.201 --> 00:15:00.904
I can't go back to my apartment.

00:15:00.964 --> 00:15:10.771
My pictures in the newspaper and, yes, I know, says Mike.

00:15:10.831 --> 00:15:13.402
It's okay.

00:15:13.462 --> 00:15:15.816
Come in.

00:15:15.876 --> 00:15:19.118
Where's the girl?

00:15:19.178 --> 00:15:20.990
asks Mike.

00:15:21.050 --> 00:15:23.171
Do you know?

00:15:23.232 --> 00:15:25.033
No.

00:15:25.093 --> 00:15:27.214
Says Greg.

00:15:27.274 --> 00:15:31.468
What can you remember about her?

00:15:31.528 --> 00:15:33.410
Says Mike.

00:15:33.470 --> 00:15:38.863
There must be something to help you find her.

00:15:38.923 --> 00:15:43.626
Yes, Greg says suddenly.

00:15:43.686 --> 00:15:46.164
Her key.

00:15:46.224 --> 00:15:52.263
A key to a room in the Dolphin Hotel.

00:15:52.323 --> 00:15:59.558
It's a small, cheap hotel near 42nd Street.

00:15:59.618 --> 00:16:03.962
She must be staying there.

00:16:04.022 --> 00:16:06.964
What's the time?

00:16:07.024 --> 00:16:12.485
Nearly nine o'clock, says Mike.

00:16:12.545 --> 00:16:18.224
Maybe she's there now, says Greg.

00:16:18.284 --> 00:16:21.344
I have to go.

00:16:21.404 --> 00:16:24.536
Thanks, Mike.

00:16:24.596 --> 00:16:32.507
Twenty minutes later, Greg is near the Dolphin Hotel.

00:16:32.568 --> 00:16:35.358
Am I too late?

00:16:35.418 --> 00:16:37.697
He thinks?

00:16:37.757 --> 00:16:45.398
Suddenly, Greg sees Cassie come out of the hotel.

00:16:45.458 --> 00:16:50.050
Cassie, he calls.

00:16:50.110 --> 00:16:52.322
Wait!

00:16:52.382 --> 00:16:56.494
I have to talk to you!

00:16:56.554 --> 00:17:02.788
Cassie sees him, but she doesn't stop.

00:17:02.848 --> 00:17:07.606
There is a car waiting for her.

00:17:07.666 --> 00:17:15.668
She says something to the driver and gets into it quickly.

00:17:15.728 --> 00:17:22.873
Oh no, says Greg.

00:17:22.893 --> 00:17:25.606
Here, 83.

00:17:25.666 --> 00:17:30.088
Says an old man in the street.

00:17:30.148 --> 00:17:33.541
Greg looks at him.

00:17:33.601 --> 00:17:35.741
What?

00:17:35.802 --> 00:17:52.350
The girl is going to peer 83 West 42nd Street for the Circle Line boat.

00:17:52.410 --> 00:17:55.612
Says the old man.

00:17:55.672 --> 00:17:58.774
Greg smiles.

00:17:58.834 --> 00:18:02.816
Thanks, he says.

00:18:02.876 --> 00:18:07.028
And he begins to run.

00:18:07.088 --> 00:18:14.472
Greg runs all the way to peer 83.

00:18:14.532 --> 00:18:19.355
People are getting on to the boat.

00:18:19.415 --> 00:18:23.528
And he gets a ticket.

00:18:23.588 --> 00:18:30.112
On the boat, Greg looks for Cassie.

00:18:30.172 --> 00:18:35.979
But a woman with a newspaper is looking at him.

00:18:36.039 --> 00:18:39.864
It's the young man in the picture.

00:18:39.924 --> 00:18:43.154
She tells the man with her.

00:18:43.214 --> 00:18:47.316
Call the police, Eddie.

00:18:47.376 --> 00:18:54.428
The man gets his phone and calls the police.

00:18:54.488 --> 00:19:00.939
Some time later, Greg sees Cassie.

00:19:00.999 --> 00:19:04.988
She is talking to a man.

00:19:05.048 --> 00:19:12.738
But Greg does not see two policemen get on the boat.

00:19:12.798 --> 00:19:17.060
They quickly find Greg.

00:19:17.120 --> 00:19:21.942
Where are Jake Russo's sketchbooks?

00:19:22.002 --> 00:19:26.024
The first policeman asks him.

00:19:26.084 --> 00:19:31.766
I don't have them, says Greg.

00:19:31.827 --> 00:19:34.823
You don't want me.

00:19:34.883 --> 00:19:38.158
You want her.

00:19:38.218 --> 00:19:42.449
She has the sketchbooks.

00:19:42.509 --> 00:19:45.750
Hey, look.

00:19:45.810 --> 00:19:48.130
He's right.

00:19:48.190 --> 00:19:51.911
Says the second policeman.

00:19:51.971 --> 00:20:00.312
The two policemen move quickly to Cassie and the man.

00:20:00.332 --> 00:20:02.563
I don't understand.

00:20:02.623 --> 00:20:04.544
Says Cassie.

00:20:04.604 --> 00:20:06.256
How?

00:20:06.316 --> 00:20:14.350
The two of you are coming with us, says one of the policemen.

00:20:14.410 --> 00:20:18.272
You're in trouble.

00:20:18.332 --> 00:20:27.526
Later, Greg and a policeman take the sketchbooks back to the hotel.

00:20:27.586 --> 00:20:34.382
Jake Russo is very happy to see them again.

00:20:34.442 --> 00:20:43.748
I'm sorry, Mr. Russo," says Greg, and tells him everything.

00:20:43.808 --> 00:20:50.649
It's okay, says the artist, smiling.

00:20:50.709 --> 00:20:57.001
But stay away from girls with beautiful green eyes.
